# Documentation Maintenance

Documentation in this repo is a **living map of the codebase**, not a historical
record. A map that lies is worse than no map, because the next reader (human or
agent) trusts it and acts on it.

**The rule: a change that makes a document wrong is not finished until that
document is fixed, in the same commit.** Not a follow-up commit, not a TODO, not
"I'll note it in the PR description."

## Why this is mandatory

Agents load documentation to decide which files to open. When `agent-navigation.md`
points at a path that moved, the next agent either wastes context rediscovering
the tree or — worse — edits the wrong thing confidently. Doc drift compounds
silently: nothing fails, no test goes red, and the map degrades until it is
abandoned. The cost is paid by everyone after you.

## What to update

Before you finish, ask: **"did I make any sentence in `docs/` false?"** Then check
these specific triggers.

| If you changed… | You must update |
| --- | --- |
| A path, module, or package boundary | [`docs/agent-navigation.md`](../../docs/agent-navigation.md) |
| Layers, data flow, DI wiring, extension points | [`docs/architecture.md`](../../docs/architecture.md) |
| A `Settings` field, default, or the YAML schema | [`docs/configuration.md`](../../docs/configuration.md) **and** `.env.example` |
| Parser routing or supported extensions | [`docs/document-formats.md`](../../docs/document-formats.md) |
| A CLI command, flag, or exit code | [`docs/cli.md`](../../docs/cli.md) |
| Retrieval behavior, ranking, chunking | [`docs/rag-retrieval.md`](../../docs/rag-retrieval.md) |
| Eval metrics, datasets, reports, leaderboard | The matching `docs/eval*` / `docs/benchmark*` page |
| Compose, k8s, probes, trust boundaries | [`docs/deployment.md`](../../docs/deployment.md) |
| Retention, uploads, audit logs | [`docs/data-lifecycle.md`](../../docs/data-lifecycle.md) |
| Logging, metrics, tracing | [`docs/observability.md`](../../docs/observability.md) |
| The retriever plugin contract | [`docs/plugin-author-guide.md`](../../docs/plugin-author-guide.md) |
| A public contract, trust boundary, or default | A **new ADR** in [`docs/adr/`](../../docs/adr/) |

The authoritative, fuller version of this table lives in
[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) under "Documentation maintenance for agents".

## Rules for writing docs here

- **Reference, don't duplicate.** State a fact in exactly one document and link
  to it from everywhere else. Two copies of a fact means one of them is already
  wrong; you just don't know which yet.
- **If you move content, it must get equal or more detail** at the destination.
  Relocating is fine; quietly shrinking is data loss.
- **Never hand-maintain what a tool generates.** API endpoints come from the
  FastAPI OpenAPI page at `/docs`; do not transcribe route tables into Markdown,
  because they drift the moment someone adds a route.
- **Verify paths and names before you write them.** Every file path, setting
  name, and command in a doc must exist. Check, don't recall.
- **One sentence per line** in Markdown prose. It keeps diffs readable and
  reviewable; there is no line-length limit to satisfy in Markdown.
- **Delete docs that describe removed behavior.** A stale page is a liability,
  not an archive — Git already keeps the history.

## Self-check before finishing

1. Did I move, rename, or delete a file? → grep the repo for its old path.
2. Did I add or change a `Settings` field? → `docs/configuration.md` + `.env.example`.
3. Did I add a command, route, format, or flag? → its reference doc.
4. Did I set or move a contract or default? → write the ADR.
5. Do all links I touched still resolve?

The last one is mechanical, so just run it:

```bash
grep -oE '\]\(([^)#][^)]*)\)' FILE.md | sed -E 's/^\]\(//; s/\)$//' |
  sed 's/#.*//' | while read -r p; do
    case "$p" in http*|"") continue;; esac
    [ -e "$(dirname FILE.md)/$p" ] || echo "BROKEN: $p"
  done
```
